<!--
  The launcher foreground: the mark's glyph, on its own, drawn dark against the
  cyan background layer. That is what the mark looks like at icon size on the
  site's own icon, which is a cyan field with the glyph knocked out of it.

  The path is the second, third and fourth subpaths of nox-logo.svg, byte for
  byte. The first subpath is the badge around them, and an icon that keeps it
  draws a rounded square inside the launcher's own rounded square with a small
  glyph lost in the middle. Nothing here is redrawn or traced.

  One scale factor for both axes. The glyph is 190 by 206, so its height sets
  the scale and its width follows, which puts 62 of the 108 canvas inside the
  66 the launcher guarantees.
-->
